  <img decoding="async" width="768" height="432" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/dogewwwww-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="Dogecoin's Downward Slide: 2 Month Stats Show Meme-Based Crypto Is Down 76%" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/dogewwwww-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/dogewwwww-300x169.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/dogewwwww-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/dogewwwww-696x385.jpg 696w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/dogewwwww-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/dogewwwww-747x420.jpg 747w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/dogewwwww-190x107.jpg 190w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/dogewwwww-380x214.jpg 380w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/dogewwwww-760x428.jpg 760w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/dogewwwww.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>The infamous meme-based crypto asset dogecoin has had an incredible 12 months, rising more than 5,578% against the U.S. dollar. Dogecoin also ignited significant demand for a number of canine-themed cryptocurrencies this year as billions of dollars have funneled into these meme-coin economies. However, in recent times the original dogecoin has faltered, and over the last three months has shed 46.24% of its value.</strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2>
    Despite Being Down 76% Since the Meme Token’s All-Time High, 12-Month Stats Show Dogecoin Is Still up Over 5,000%
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    For many years, dogecoin (DOGE) spent its life trading below a U.S. penny — from 2014 all the way until January 2021. But much to the co-creator of dogecoin’s dismay, DOGE has surged in value during the last year against the U.S. dollar, gaining a whopping 5,578%.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Against bitcoin (BTC), DOGE has jumped 1,551% over the last 12 months. Still, after all those gains dogecoin has slid immensely in value following the rest of the crypto market’s downturn.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" srcset="https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/tbcmtxdq-300x198.png 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/tbcmtxdq-768x508.png 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/tbcmtxdq-1024x677.png 1024w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/tbcmtxdq-1536x1015.png 1536w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/tbcmtxdq-2048x1354.png 2048w, https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/tbcmtxdq.png 2160w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2160px) 100vw, 2160px" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-475279 size-full" title="Dogecoin's Downward Slide: 2-Month Stats Show Meme-Based Crypto Is Down 76%" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/tbcmtxdq.png" alt="Dogecoin's Downward Slide: 2-Month Stats Show Meme-Based Crypto Is Down 76%" width="2160" height="1428" />On Saturday, July 17, dogecoin (DOGE) has been trading for $0.17 per unit after reaching $0.737 per unit two months ago. The well-known meme crypto is now down more than 76% from the crypto asset’s all-time high (ATH). Seven-day statistics show DOGE has lost 18% this week, and 30-day stats show a loss of more than 43% during the last month.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Dogecoin still has a very large market capitalization with $23 billion at the time of writing. The DOGE market cap is much larger than the coin’s ERC20 competitor, shiba inu (SHIB), which has a $3.3 billion market valuation today.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <h2>
    Baby Doge Sheds 63% This Week, Yooshi Token and Elondoge Gather This Week’s Double-Digit Meme Token Gains
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    In terms of percentages down from the ATH, dogecoin is down a lot more than many coins in the top twenty positions. Compared to dogecoin’s competitors like SHIB, dogecoin lost more weekly gains than SHIB’s 15% losses this past week.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    However, baby doge (BABYDOGE) has lost a massive 63.2% this week. All the canine meme tokens have seen deep losses and only a few meme tokens have done well. A meme-crypto asset called yooshi (YOOSHI) has been the only big gainer, gathering 57% this week.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" srcset="https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/yooshi-300x169.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/yooshi-768x432.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/yooshi-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/yooshi.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-475281 size-full" title="Dogecoin's Downward Slide: 2-Month Stats Show Meme-Based Crypto Is Down 76%" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/yooshi.jpg" alt="Dogecoin's Downward Slide: 2-Month Stats Show Meme-Based Crypto Is Down 76%" width="1280" height="720" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    YOOSHI is not a dog coin, as it looks more like a frog, but the token community that claims to boast 220K members aims to create a metaverse, NFTs, and also to give to charity. Finally, a relatively unknown dog coin called Elondoge token (EDOGE) has gained double digits this week with a 28% rise.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    It’s hard to say what the meme-based token economy will do from here, but it seems these coins are falling victim to the overall market sentiment no matter how colorful they are.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <em><strong>What do you think about dogecoin’s market performance in recent times and the other meme-based crypto assets? Let us know what you think about this subject in the comments section below. </strong></em>
  </p>
